{"title":"Career roadmap — Screenwriter","role":"Screenwriter","summary":"A Screenwriter develops stories and writes scripts for films, television, streaming platforms, web series, animation, games and other screen-based media. The career is primarily portfolio- and craft-driven: a strong screenplay, storytelling ability, industry understanding and professional network generally matter more than collecting qualifications.","facts":{"Current degree":"BA (Bachelor of Arts – General / Honours)","Course":"Creative Writing / Film Studies / Screenwriting"},"about":[],"intro":[],"horizons":[],"sections":[{"heading":"Career horizons","kind":"horizons","blocks":[{"type":"table","header":["Period","Career focus"],"rows":[[{"text":"2026–2030"},{"text":"Master storytelling, screenplay structure, character development, dialogue and visual writing"}],[{"text":"2030–2035"},{"text":"Build credits through short films, web series, production houses, writers' rooms and independent projects"}],[{"text":"2035–2040"},{"text":"Become a professional screenwriter, story developer, series writer or writer-producer"}],[{"text":"2040–2046"},{"text":"Lead writers' rooms, create original IP, become a showrunner/creative producer or establish a production company"}]]}]},{"heading":"What to build each year","kind":"build","blocks":[{"type":"h","text":"Year 1 — Storytelling foundation"},{"type":"p","text":"Study:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Story structure"},{"text":"Character development"},{"text":"Plot and conflict"},{"text":"Theme"},{"text":"Dialogue"},{"text":"Scene construction"},{"text":"Point of view"},{"text":"Genre"},{"text":"Visual storytelling"},{"text":"Film language"},{"text":"World-building"}]},{"type":"p","text":"Read and analyse:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Feature-film screenplays"},{"text":"Television scripts"},{"text":"Web-series scripts"},{"text":"Short-film scripts"},{"text":"Stage plays"},{"text":"Adapted screenplays"}]},{"type":"p","text":"Write regularly:"},{"t