},{"text":"Regional-language content"},{"text":"International co-productions"}]},{"type":"h","text":"2. AI + Screenwriting"},{"type":"p","text":"AI tools may increasingly assist with:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Brainstorming"},{"text":"Research"},{"text":"Character alternatives"},{"text":"Story structure analysis"},{"text":"Continuity checking"},{"text":"Script coverage"},{"text":"Translation/localisation"}]},{"type":"p","text":"But original voice, human experience, creative judgement and final authorship remain central."},{"type":"h","text":"3. Interactive Storytelling"},{"type":"p","text":"Screenwriters can move into:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Video games"},{"text":"Interactive films"},{"text":"Virtual worlds"},{"text":"Immersive theatre"},{"text":"AR/VR narratives"}]},{"type":"p","text":"The major difference is that stories can have multiple branches and user-driven outcomes."},{"type":"h","text":"4. Transmedia Storytelling"},{"type":"p","text":"One story universe can extend across:"},{"type":"flow","items":["Film","Series","Games","Comics","Podcasts","Interactive experiences"]},{"type":"p","text":"Writers who understand IP development will have an advantage."},{"type":"h","text":"5. Regional-language storytelling"},{"type":"p","text":"Strong opportunities can emerge from writers who can combine:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Local culture"},{"text":"Authentic dialogue"},{"text":"Regional history"},{"text":"Contemporary themes"},{"text":"Global storytelling standards"}]},{"type":"h","text":"6. Writer-Producer Careers"},{"type":"p","text":"More writers may increasingly control:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Story development"},{"text":"Casting concepts"},{"text":"Production decisions"},{"text":"IP development"},{"text":"Distribution strategy"},{"text":"Franchise expansion"}]},{"type":"note","label":"2040–2046","text":"How the role evolves"},{"type":"p","text":"The screenwriter increasingly becomes a story architect rather than simply someone who writes pages."},{"type":"p","text":"A senior professional may manage:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Story universes"},{"text":"Writers' rooms"},{"text":"Character franchises"},{"text":"Multi-season narratives"},{"text":"Film/series adaptations"},{"text":"Interactive narratives"},{"text":"AI-assisted development"},{"text":"International localisation"}]},{"type":"p","text":"The strongest future profile will combine:"},{"type":"flow","items":["Writing","Story Development","Production","IP","Technology"],"sep":"+"},{"type":"h","text":"Recommended final skill stack"},{"type":"h","text":"Writing"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Storytelling"},{"text":"Screenplay structure"},{"text":"Character development"},{"text":"Dialogue"},{"text":"Scene construction"},{"text":"Rewriting"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Film"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Film language"},{"text":"Cinematography basics"},{"text":"Editing"},{"text":"Directing fundamentals"},{"text":"Production workflow"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Professional"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Pitching"},{"text":"Story bibles"},{"text":"Treatments"},{"text":"Collaboration"},{"text":"Contract/IP awareness"},{"text":"Industry networking"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Technology"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Screenwriting software"},{"text":"Digital production"},{"text":"AI-assisted research"},{"text":"Video editing"},{"text":"Storyboarding"},{"text":"Multimedia storytelling"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Business"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Copyright"},{"text":"IP development"},{"text":"Pitch decks"},{"text":"Production economics"},{"text":"Streaming business models"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Target progression"},{"type":"flow","items":["Creative writing + film fundamentals","2027–28: Screenplay craft + regular scriptwriting","2028–29: Short films + feature/series portfolio","2029–30: Industry internship + professional networking","2030–32: Writer's room / Script Assistant / Junior Writer","2032–35: Professional Screenwriter / Series Writer","2035–40: Senior Writer / Story Editor / Writer-Producer","2040–46: Showrunner / Creator / Executive Producer / Production Entrepreneur"],"label":"2026–27:"},{"type":"h","text":"Best employability combination"},{"type":"flow","items":["BA Creative Writing/Film Studies","Professional Screenwriting Training","Strong Portfolio","Short-Film/Series Credits","Writers' Room Experience","Pitching","IP/Production Knowledge"],"sep":"+"},{"type":"note","label":"Key principle","text":"Screenwriting is one of the most portfolio-driven careers in the humanities. The degree provides a foundation, but employability is primarily demonstrated through excellent scripts, original ideas, completed projects, writing credits, collaboration skills and the ability to rewrite a story until it works on screen."}]}]}